{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337101-stealing-hearthstones-question","id":1337101,"title":"Stealing Hearthstones question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-20T08:41:22-07:00","id":1337101,"title":"Stealing Hearthstones question","content":"If your solar exalt defeated some dragon-blooded punk and found that the DB had a hearthstone socketed into an amulet on him, I know the solar could take that hearthstone and use it as he pleases. But assume that its linked to a manse somewhere far away, the Blessed isle or somewhere. Could the dragon-blooded's family cut the hearthstone off by taking over the manse? Is there anyway to stop someone from using your manses hearthstone if they have it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T08:56:15-07:00","id":1337103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337101-stealing-hearthstones-question#post1337101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your solar exalt defeated some dragon-blooded punk and found that the DB had a hearthstone socketed into an amulet on him, I know the solar could take that hearthstone and use it as he pleases. But assume that its linked to a manse somewhere far away, the Blessed isle or somewhere. Could the dragon-blooded's family cut the hearthstone off by taking over the manse? Is there anyway to stop someone from using your manses hearthstone if they have it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, they just have to reform the heartstone at the manse. Multiple people can be attuned to a manse if I recall. So it's just a matter of having the hearthroom form a new hearthstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T12:52:23-07:00","id":1337137,"title":"","content":"It should be a simple task for a skilled geomancer with full access to the manse to &quot;break&quot; the previous stone and get a new one formed. it will probably take a while though, hearthstones don't usually form overnight and manses don't destabilize with the flip of a switch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T23:33:26-07:00","id":1337217,"title":"","content":"The core rules address this. Linked Hearthstones can be destroyed by heavily damaging (or destroying) the manse, where upon the stone will become inert and crumble to ash within days. After being repaired, the manse will generate a new Hearthstone over the course of the next season.<br /> <br /> Steady Hearthstones are not so easily destroyed, as they are independent of the state of their Manse or Demesne.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I'd be more interested in the possibility of someone using the Manse to locate the Hearthstone (or <i>vice versa</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-21-2019, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T05:22:58-07:00","id":1337233,"title":"","content":"Rules wise I'd call it a major project akin to repairing the manse.<br /> <br /> And yeah, using the manse to track the stone might be an interesting trick. I would give it some severe limitations though. it shouldn't be precise enough that you can tell, say, which city the stone is in. A good test might tell you the stone is in the river province, or the wavecrest archipelago. Wherever it points, it's still a wiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiide search radius. Like, several dozens of kilometers radius.<br /> This way it's not a scrying gps while still allowing you to fast track investigators into the general area where rumors might spread in a timely fashion and most wilderness evidence isn't fully eroded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T06:09:31-07:00","id":1337240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337101-stealing-hearthstones-question?p=1337233#post1337233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This way it's not a scrying gps while still allowing you to fast track investigators into the general area where rumors might spread in a timely fashion and most wilderness evidence isn't fully eroded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chances are if you're a Dragon-Blooded then your manse is on the Blessed Isle, the Anathema that took the Hearthstone is <i>thousands</i> of miles away, and if you're supremely well connected you might be able to travel at speeds of a hundred miles per hour.<br /> <br /> I think a couple of city blocks is probably inaccurate enough when you consider it'll be weeks before you get there.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Perception + Occult ritual taking three hours inside the Manse. 5 successes narrows it to a few city blocks. 3 successes the city. 1 success the vague to the tune of several dozen kilometers. 0 successes the Direction (&quot;the Hearthstone is somewhere in... the West&quot;). Botch for inaccurate information. (A three hour ritual time stops you Infallible Messengering your agents on the Threshold with GPS updates.)<br /> <br /> (Also, RAW repairing a Manse is a <i>Superior</i> project requiring upto <i>a year</i> depending on the severity of the damage.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-21-2019, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T08:05:05-07:00","id":1337247,"title":"","content":"I estimated major instead of superior because you're not really <i>repairing a broken manse</i>, just working it to break the stone and then back. It's a far more controlled and contained task.<br /> <br /> And on the accuracy...<br /> How resourceful can you expect the typical geomancer to be? The Realm doesn't like its sorcerers, but will sure as hell use them. If it's something as serious as a dynast-endorsed wyld hunt, or even a &quot;the matriarch personally ordered us to gut that thief and strangle him with his own intestines&quot; scenario, you can expect daily updates regardless of distance.<br /> <br /> I'm quite fine with a more vague tracking than that you suggest. A minor warlord that happens to have a couple decent thaumaturges and a geomancer doesn't strike me as a person who should be able to track you down that precisely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T14:34:46-07:00","id":1337268,"title":"","content":"So to conclude a sensible house rule then:<br /> The link between a hearthstone and its manse can be broken by a skilled geomancer or by causing enough damage to the manse, merely being attuned does not let you sever the connection. The manse regenerates its hearthstone, usually over the course of about a season, although if the manse was damaged, this will need to be repaired first, a major project (less than described in the books since the damage was surgical and the repairer knows exactly what needs to be fixed, i.e. the exact thing they broke). <br /> Until the manse is damaged or the connection severed, the hearthstone works just as well for the cheeky exalt that nicked it as it did for the DB he took it from. But a geomancer could use the manse as a link to the hearthstone to find the exalt, possibly scrying on them or determining their location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}